message: "If you use this software or its derived data, please cite it as below."
title: "Water Stress, Fragile Institutions, and Unrest in Syria (2000-2012): Earth Engine scripts and indicator matrix"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ventura
    given-names: Sean
    affiliation: "USC Spatial Sciences Institute"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/VentGit573/syria-water-stress-geoint"
keywords:
  - Syria
  - drought
  - Google Earth Engine
  - remote sensing
  - human security
  - GEOINT
  - indicator matrix
abstract: >-
  Google Earth Engine and Python scripts, with small derived district-level
  tables, for analysing Syria's 2006-2010 drought, crop and water stress,
  night-light and settlement change, and their relationship to the 2011
  uprising through a weighted strain/indicator matrix. Scripts drafted with
  Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic) and run and adjusted by the author.
